   "source": [
    "# F1 Lap Time Prediction from Tire Age\n",
    "\n",
    "Predicts in-race lap times from tire age, using the Formula 1 World Championship (1950–2020) dataset (`results.csv`, `races.csv`, `pit_stops.csv`, `lap_times.csv`). Run top to bottom; the four CSVs must sit in the same folder as this notebook (or set `F1_DATA_DIR`).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Leakage audit note:** every statistic used to clean or prepare the modeling data (the 1.5×-median outlier threshold) is computed from each driver's **training partition only** (their earlier stints) and then applied unchanged to that driver's test partition (final stint) — the same fit-on-train / apply-to-test pattern as fitting a scaler. The only lap-time statistics computed on the pooled field *before* any split exist purely to screen which **race** to analyze (Section 2) — at that point no train/test split exists yet, so there is nothing for that step to leak into."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "ae1c1228",
   "metadata": {
