   "source": [
    "### Leak-free per-driver cleaning helper\n",
    "Defined here (ahead of race ranking) because race/driver **eligibility** itself depends on whether a driver survives cleaning with a non-empty train *and* test partition — and that check must use the same leak-free rule as the final analysis, not a shortcut.\n",
    "\n",
    "The function: (1) removes pit-stop laps and post-pit laps — structural, based only on pit-stop lap numbers, so this step cannot leak lap-time information; (2) assigns `stint_id` and splits into the driver's earlier-stint (train) and final-stint (test) rows; (3) computes the 1.5×-median outlier threshold **from the train rows only**; (4) applies that same train-derived threshold to both train and test rows. A driver is only usable if both partitions remain non-empty afterward."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "2620a4b5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T10:00:21.256099Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T10:00:21.255527Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T10:00:21.263334Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T10:00:21.262408Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def clean_driver_laps_noleak(rid, drv, laps_df, pits_df):\n",
    "    ldf = laps_df[(laps_df.raceId == rid) & (laps_df.driverId == drv)].sort_values(\"lap\").copy()\n",
    "    if len(ldf) == 0:\n",
    "        return None, dict(n_pit=0, n_post=0, n_slow_train=0, n_slow_test=0, train_median=None)\n",
    "    pit_laps = sorted(pits_df[(pits_df.raceId == rid) & (pits_df.driverId == drv)][\"lap\"].tolist())\n",
    "\n",
    "    # --- structural cleaning: depends only on pit-stop lap numbers, not lap-time values ---\n",
    "    ldf[\"is_pit_lap\"] = ldf[\"lap\"].isin(pit_laps)\n",
    "    n_pit = int(ldf[\"is_pit_lap\"].sum())\n",
    "    step1 = ldf[~ldf[\"is_pit_lap\"]].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    post_pit_set = {p + 1 for p in pit_laps}\n",
    "    step1[\"is_post_pit\"] = step1[\"lap\"].isin(post_pit_set)\n",
    "    n_post = int(step1[\"is_post_pit\"].sum())\n",
    "    step2 = step1[~step1[\"is_post_pit\"]].copy()\n",
    "    if len(step2) == 0:\n",
    "        return step2, dict(n_pit=n_pit, n_post=n_post, n_slow_train=0, n_slow_test=0, train_median=None)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # --- stint split BEFORE any lap-time statistic is computed ---\n",
    "    step2[\"stint_id\"] = step2[\"lap\"].apply(lambda L: len([p for p in pit_laps if p < L]))\n",
    "    max_stint = step2[\"stint_id\"].max()\n",
    "    train_part = step2[step2.stint_id < max_stint].copy()\n",
    "    test_part = step2[step2.stint_id == max_stint].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if len(train_part) == 0:\n",
    "        # no earlier-stint data -> no valid training statistic -> driver unusable\n",
    "        return None, dict(n_pit=n_pit, n_post=n_post, n_slow_train=0, n_slow_test=0, train_median=None)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # --- TRAIN-ONLY statistic, applied identically to train and test (fit-on-train / transform-both) ---\n",
    "    train_median = float(train_part[\"milliseconds\"].median())\n",
    "    train_part[\"slow_flag\"] = train_part[\"milliseconds\"] > 1.5 * train_median\n",
    "    n_slow_train = int(train_part[\"slow_flag\"].sum())\n",
    "    train_clean = train_part[~train_part[\"slow_flag\"]].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    test_part[\"slow_flag\"] = test_part[\"milliseconds\"] > 1.5 * train_median\n",
    "    n_slow_test = int(test_part[\"slow_flag\"].sum())\n",
    "    test_clean = test_part[~test_part[\"slow_flag\"]].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    counts = dict(n_pit=n_pit, n_post=n_post, n_slow_train=n_slow_train, n_slow_test=n_slow_test, train_median=train_median)\n",
    "    if len(train_clean) == 0 or len(test_clean) == 0:\n",
    "        return None, counts\n",
    "\n",
    "    combined = pd.concat([train_clean, test_clean]).sort_values(\"lap\")\n",
    "    return combined, counts\n"
   ]
  },
