    "## 4. Feature engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "**`tire_age` convention:** resets to 0 at the pit-stop lap; each completed lap afterward adds 1 (so the out-lap `P+1` would be `tire_age = 1`). Because cleaning removes both the pit lap and the out-lap, the first retained lap of a new stint is `P+2`, with `tire_age = 2` (verified below). Before any stop, `tire_age` counts from the race start (lap 1 → `tire_age = 1`).\n",
    "\n",
    "`tire_age` and `grid` depend only on pit-stop lap numbers and starting grid position — not on lap-time values — so neither is a leakage concern."
